1.3 "Outreach Services" shall mean the community health education sessions, routine immunisation demand generation, referral tracking, and related activities described in the Scope of Work attached as Annex A.

1.4 "Target Wards" shall mean the specific administrative wards listed in Annex B, as may be amended from time to time by mutual written agreement of the parties.

1.5 "Effective Date" shall mean the date of execution of this Agreement, being 15/01/2025.

1.6 "Term" shall mean the period commencing on 15/01/2025 and expiring on 31/12/2025, unless earlier terminated in accordance with Article 12.

ARTICLE 2: APPOINTMENT AND SCOPE OF WORK

2.1 The Board hereby appoints the Implementing NGO to plan, coordinate, and deliver the Outreach Services in the Target Wards, and the Implementing NGO accepts the appointment.

2.2 The principal components of the Outreach Services are:

(a) Conduct of community dialogue sessions and health education talks in each Target Ward, with a minimum of two (2) sessions per ward per quarter;

(b) Identification and training of community health volunteers (CHVs), with a target of at least ten (10) trained and active volunteers per Target Ward;

(c) Demand generation for routine immunisation, including defaulters tracing and defaulter tracking using the standard registers provided by the Board;

(d) Referral of pregnant women, children under five, and other priority groups to the nearest functional primary health care facility, with a documented referral slip and follow-up within seven (7) days;

(e) Monthly data collation and submission of activity reports to the Board's Monitoring and Evaluation Unit in the format prescribed by the Board;

