(f) Participation in quarterly review meetings convened by the Board.

2.3 The Implementing NGO shall not undertake any activity outside the scope of work without the prior written approval of the Board.

ARTICLE 3: OBLIGATIONS OF THE IMPLEMENTING NGO

3.1 The Implementing NGO shall:

(a) Deploy qualified and trained personnel to manage the outreach activities, including a Programme Manager, at least two (2) Field Supervisors, and such number of Community Health Extension Workers (CHEWs) as may be required for the effective delivery of the services;

(b) Ensure that all personnel deployed under this Agreement comply with the Board's code of conduct, including punctuality, professional dress, and respectful communication with community members;

(c) Maintain accurate and up-to-date records of all outreach activities, including attendance registers, session reports, referral logs, and training records;

(d) Submit monthly narrative and financial reports to the Board not later than the fifth (5th) day of the following month;

(e) Procure and maintain all non-medical supplies required for the outreach activities, including but not limited to flip charts, megaphones, branded materials, and stationery;

(f) Safeguard any data or personal information of community members obtained during the course of the Outreach Services, and use such data solely for the purposes of this Agreement;

(g) Immediately notify the Board of any incident, accident, or security concern arising in the course of the outreach activities that may affect the delivery of services.
